shader: shadow the data register of STG.U and ISBEWR

The check that decides whether an instruction needs shadow registers skips bits 32-39
unless the opcode is on a short list, and neither 0x986 (STG with a uniform address)
nor 0x927 (ISBEWR) was on it. PrepareRegisterPressure already handles both. So a store
whose data sat in R216-R245 stored the lowering's own uniform mirror, with no error,
and data in R246 and up failed "native global store size".

0x927: Lichii PR 100, c6f190548 by Zarigis. Ocarina's mesh 8159e91e0097876a stores R238
and R240; the wrong value was a NaN on Link's door that bloom turned into a white glow.
0x986: Lichii PR 65, d9748a5d5 by Zortos (Kirby white world). Its test uses a captured
STG with data in R250.

No effect on a program without such a store. Lichii's 0x987 is left out: not lowered
here.

diff --git a/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h b/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
index b9dccac..db69d14 100644
--- a/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
+++ b/src/shader_recompiler/frontend/ampere/lower_to_maxwell.h
@@ -265,7 +265,7 @@ inline LoweredProgram LowerToMaxwellWith(std::span<const Instruction> code, u32
         bool requires_shadow = false;
         for (u32 bit : {16U, 24U, 32U, 64U}) {
             if (bit == 32 && insn.Bits(9, 3) != 1 && opcode != 0xb60 && opcode != 0xb66 && opcode != 0xf66 &&
-                opcode != 0x988) continue;
+                opcode != 0x988 && opcode != 0x986 && opcode != 0x927) continue;
             const u32 reg = insn.Bits(bit, 8);
             if (reg >= shadow_boundary && reg < 255) requires_shadow = true;
         }
